        "original_id": "59d38656-2867-5e2d-ab71-60ee0b165fa4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kerry Saxby-Junna, Cathy Freeman, Jana Pittman, Sally Pearson, Dimitri Markov, Jared Tallent, Mitchell Watt\n- Places: Young, New South Wales; Ballina, New South Wales; Parap, Northern Territory; Darwin, Northern Territory; Australia\n- Topics: Australia at the World Championships in Athletics; 2011 census\n\nFacts:\n- Kerry Saxby-Junna was born in Young, New South Wales, and grew up in Ballina, New South Wales.\n- At the 2011 census, Young, New South Wales, had a population of 6,960.\n- Cathy Freeman, Jana Pittman, and Sally Pearson are Australia's only multiple gold medal winners at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Cathy Freeman won a bronze medal, and Sally Pearson won a silver medal, in addition to their multiple World Championships gold medals for Australia.\n- Dimitri Markov won 1 gold medal and 1 silver medal for Australia at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Jared Tallent won 1 silver medal and 2 bronze medals for Australia at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Kerry Saxby-Junna won 1 silver medal and 1 bronze medal for Australia at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Mitchell Watt won 1 silver medal and 1 bronze medal for Australia at the World Championships in Athletics.\n- Parap is an inner suburb of Darwin, Northern Territory, Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
